title: Commonwealth intervention of Stathmore
subtitle: History repeats itself.
view-if: reichsexekution_defeated = 0 and president = "DuFour" and red_thuringia and (banner_force + vanguard_force < 75) and not presidential_powers and (heartland_coup_seen or heartland_reichsexekution or dufour_angry >= 100 or dufour_angry_bruning >= 50 or strife >= 5 or banner_militancy >= 0.1 or bruning_time or saxony_joever) and year >= 1930
on-arrival: thuringia_joever = 1; strife += 1; dufour_angry += 25; dufour_angry_bruning -= 25
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/Commonwealth Army.jpg

= Commonwealth intervention of Stathmore

President [+ president +] has invoked the <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> to dismiss the Stathmore government, citing its "inability to maintain order" amidst escalating clashes between the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, the Banners, and the increasingly militant <span style="color: #700000;">**Vanguard**</span>.

However, the true motivation is clear: the left-wing coalition governing Stathmore poses a direct threat to the conservative and nationalist establishment in the Commonwealth.

- @defend
- @surrender

@defend
title: Fight against this overthrow attempt!
subtitle: Labor will call a general strike. The Banners and Vanguard will be mobilized to resist the Commonwealth Army. 

The Commonwealth Army and the Wardens are already preparing to enter Stathmore. Our forces are unprepared for a fight and many Reformists think that the risk of civl war over Stathmore is too high. Do we recognize this?

- @defend_2: We will defend the Stathmore Government with the Collectivists. 
- @surrender

@defend_2
on-arrival: resist_coup = 1; thuringia_joever = 0; reformist_dissent += 10; defense_strength = banner_strength*banner_militancy*(1-dissent/2); defense_strength += vanguard_strength*vanguard_militancy; defense_strength += commons_marcher_normalized*(1 - dissent)*(2 - disfavored/100); defense_strength += commons_collectivist_normalized*(2 - disfavored/100); defense_strength *= 0.8; enemy_strength = loyalist_strength*loyalist_militancy + warden_strength*warden_militancy; enemy_strength += army_strength*army_militancy*(1-army_loyalty)
go-to: defend_2_civil_war if defense_strength < enemy_strength; defend_2_victory if defense_strength >= enemy_strength

@defend_2_civil_war

As the Commonwealth Army and their reactionary auxiliaries march into Stathmore, armed fighting erupts between them and the leftist forces of the Stathmore government. DuFour refuses to withdraw the Commonwealth intervention and orders more Commonwealth Army troops into Stathmore.  

- @civil_war: It is a civil war.

@defend_2_victory
on-arrival: loyalist_strength *= 0.8; warden_strength *= 0.8; left_dissent -= 10; reformist_dissent -= 10; reichsexekution_defeated = 1; pro_republic += 5; commons_marcher += 4; disfavored_marcher += 4; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_collectivist += 3; commons_royalist -= 6; disfavored_royalist -= 6; dufour_angry -= 35; dufour_angry_bruning += 30; coup_victory = 1; collectivist_relation += 15; vanguard_strength += 100; vanguard_militancy += 0.1; banner_strength += 200
achievement: drei_pfeile

The Banners and Vanguard confront the reactionaries on the road to Stathmore and somehow, the enemy has retreated without a fight! They were surprised by our resistance and DuFour has decided to not risk a civil war over Stathmore.

This show of force has reinvigorated support for both the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and has weakened the Sovereigntists and reactionaries. DuFour's ire has also been turned away from us. For now. 

@surrender
title: Resign our positions, to prevent bloodshed.
subtitle: DuFour will appoint a new <i>Commonwealth Commissioner</i>.
on-arrival: red_thuringia = 0; commons_marcher -= 3; commons_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_marcher -= 3; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; banner_militancy = banner_militancy*0.8; banner_strength -= 200; vanguard_banned = 1; vanguard_strength -= 100; vanguard_militancy -= 0.1; collectivist_relation -= 25; communist_coalition -= 1

The <span style="color: #700000;">collectivists</span> protesting in the streets are brutally suppressed, with the Commonwealth Army patrolling the streets, restricting political gatherings, and turning a blind eye to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> as they harass local party officials.

DuFour appoints <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**FCL**</span> member Hewlin Brae as <i>Commonwealth Commissioner</i> to govern Stathmore, tasked with dismantling our reforms and violently suppressing the <span style="color: #700000;">**Vanguard**</span>.
